            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0303" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 1518/72–73.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>,<date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-09-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 28, 1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 742.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith an
                    edict of Her Imperial Majesty the Empress Dowager, published on the 20th
                    instant, taking the first step looking to the calling of what I think may be
                    considered as a constituent or constitutional assembly, although some doubt
                    still exists as to the exact duties to be performed by the “Tzu Cheng Yuan.” The
                    choice of officials to preside over it is, to say <pb facs="0304" n="192"
                        xml:id="pg192"/> the least, curious—the prince a young, intelligent, but
                    untried man (he was recently, you will recollect, appointed a probationer in the
                    Grand Council, the first office of importance he has held), the other a
                    venerable statesman of 80, who has passed all his official career in Peking,
                    where he has held offices in most of the departments of Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d163-a1.xml" xpointer="d163-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
